							<section class="entry-content">
	
<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<p>Our Fantasy Premier League (FPL) 2026/27 <a href="https://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/category/pre-season/team-guides">team previews</a> continue with Brighton and Hove Albion.</p>



<p>Here, we discuss their best FPL picks for the upcoming campaign, predict the line-up for Gameweek 1, review pre-season, detail their set-piece takers, assess the summer transfer activity and more.</p>



<div class="wp-block-cover wp-duotone-unset-1" style="min-height:100px;aspect-ratio:unset;"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim" style="background-color:#304e3c"></span><picture><source srcset="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/image-2026-07-24T120104.598.webp 1080w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/image-2026-07-24T120104.598-240x300.webp 240w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/image-2026-07-24T120104.598-819x1024.webp 819w" sizes="(max-width: 1080px) 100vw, 1080px" type="image/webp"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1080" height="1350" class="wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-172739 webpexpress-processed" alt="The Only FPL Companion App You Need for 2026/27 1" src="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/image-2026-07-24T120104.598.jpg" data-object-fit="cover" srcset="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/image-2026-07-24T120104.598.jpg 1080w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/image-2026-07-24T120104.598-240x300.jpg 240w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/image-2026-07-24T120104.598-819x1024.jpg 819w" sizes="(max-width: 1080px) 100vw, 1080px"></picture><div class="wp-block-cover__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-block-cover-is-layout-constrained">
<p class="has-text-align-center has-white-color has-text-color has-link-color wp-elements-a324d042b4872a3aa2e38c2c8bb8f2dc" style="font-size:22px"><strong><a href="https://bit.ly/FFScoutEditorial">Score More Points. Win More Mini Leagues. Join FFScout.</a></strong></p>
</div></div>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">REASONS TO BE CHEERFUL</h2>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full is-resized is-style-default"><picture><source srcset="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/RTSUM361-2.webp 1000w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/RTSUM361-2-300x200.webp 300w" sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px" type="image/webp"><img decoding="async" width="1000" height="667" src="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/RTSUM361-2.jpg" alt="Fabian Hurzeler at Brighton: What we can expect in FPL 2" class="wp-image-118964 webpexpress-processed" style="object-fit:cover;width:450px;height:251px" srcset="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/RTSUM361-2.jpg 1000w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/RTSUM361-2-300x200.jpg 300w" sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px"></picture></figure>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading">A STRONG FINISH TO LAST SEASON</h4>



<p>Last season was a real rollercoaster for Brighton and Hove Albion fans.</p>



<p>From the start of December to mid-February, they took just nine points from 39, with a solitary win over Burnley in 13 matches.</p>



<p>But after that, it all seemed to click for Fabian Hurzeler’s side, with seven wins and one draw in 12 games to finish the season.</p>



<p>However, in terms of their defensive metrics, they were really solid from the start of the year.</p>



<p>From Gameweek 19, they ranked second for expected goals conceded (xGC), with 23.23 xGC:</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><picture><source srcset="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-176.webp 249w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-176-134x300.webp 134w" sizes="(max-width: 249px) 100vw, 249px" type="image/webp"><img decoding="async" width="249" height="556" src="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-176.png" alt="" class="wp-image-174196 webpexpress-processed" srcset="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-176.png 249w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-176-134x300.png 134w" sizes="(max-width: 249px) 100vw, 249px"></picture></figure>



<p></p>



<p>They were also third for fewest shots conceded (212), only behind Arsenal (178) and Manchester City (200).</p>



<p>They’ve since lost centre-back <strong>Jan Paul van Hecke</strong> (£5.0m) to Tottenham Hotspur, which is far from ideal, but they have at least replaced him with several new arrivals at the back, including <strong>Luka Vuskovic</strong> (£5.0m) and <strong>Pascal Struijk</strong> (£5.0m).</p>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading">STABILITY</h4>



<p>Hurzeler is remarkably one of the longest-serving managers in the Premier League.</p>



<p>This could provide Brighton with an early boost, particularly if the nine new top-flight managers require time to settle at their respective clubs.</p>



<p>Hurzeler already has a deep understanding of both Albion and his players, of course, having guided Brighton to back-to-back eighth-place finishes in his two seasons at the helm.</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p>“… I think now to go to my third season is definitely an advantage for me. I understand more and more the Premier League. I understand more and more my players. Of course, we added some new players. But the core, the style of play, how I want to lead and how I how build this connection with the core we already have in this club will remain the same.” – Fabian Hurzeler, <a href="https://www.wearebrighton.com/newsopinion/hurzeler-being-fifth-longest-serving-premier-league-manager-gives-brighton-an-advantage/">via We Are Brighton</a></p>
</blockquote>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">REASONS TO BE FEARFUL</h2>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-resized is-style-default"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="469" src="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/what-welbecks-move-to-chelsea-may-mean-for-pedro-brighton-assets-1024x469.jpg" alt="What Welbeck’s move to Chelsea may mean for Pedro + Brighton assets" class="wp-image-173444" style="object-fit:cover;width:452px;height:250px" srcset="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/what-welbecks-move-to-chelsea-may-mean-for-pedro-brighton-assets-1024x469.jpg 1024w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/what-welbecks-move-to-chelsea-may-mean-for-pedro-brighton-assets-300x137.jpg 300w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/what-welbecks-move-to-chelsea-may-mean-for-pedro-brighton-assets-1536x704.jpg 1536w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/what-welbecks-move-to-chelsea-may-mean-for-pedro-brighton-assets.jpg 1700w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading">A TRIP TO THE ARCTIC CIRCLE</h4>



<p>Brighton will face Norwegian outfit Tromso, who are based in the Arctic Circle, in the play-off round of the Conference League.</p>



<p>They visit Norway on Thursday 20 August, just a few days before their Gameweek 1 opener at home to Aston Villa. The second leg is at the Amex Stadium on 27 August.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-resized is-style-default"><picture><source srcset="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screen-Shot-2026-08-14-at-10.50.14-1024x607.webp 1024w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screen-Shot-2026-08-14-at-10.50.14-300x178.webp 300w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screen-Shot-2026-08-14-at-10.50.14-1536x911.webp 1536w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screen-Shot-2026-08-14-at-10.50.14-141x84.webp 141w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screen-Shot-2026-08-14-at-10.50.14.webp 1620w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" type="image/webp"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="607" src="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screen-Shot-2026-08-14-at-10.50.14-1024x607.png" alt="" class="wp-image-173922 webpexpress-processed" style="width:450px" srcset="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screen-Shot-2026-08-14-at-10.50.14-1024x607.png 1024w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screen-Shot-2026-08-14-at-10.50.14-300x178.png 300w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screen-Shot-2026-08-14-at-10.50.14-1536x911.png 1536w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screen-Shot-2026-08-14-at-10.50.14-141x84.png 141w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Screen-Shot-2026-08-14-at-10.50.14.png 1620w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px"></picture></figure>



<p></p>



<p>Hurzeler could rotate his line-ups for Europe, of course, but the quick turnarounds next season, especially at the start, are a concern for Fantasy managers.</p>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading">KEY DEPARTURES &#8211; PARTICULARLY UP TOP</h4>



<p>Brighton have lost a couple of key players this summer, in van Hecke and <strong>Danny Welbeck</strong> (£6.0m).</p>



<p>The Dutch centre-back was Albion’s best defender in 2025/26.</p>



<p>Welbeck meanwhile netted 23 Premier League goals and supplied six assists over the past two seasons.</p>



<ul>
<li><strong>READ MORE:</strong> <a href="https://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/2026/08/07/welbeck-to-chelsea-how-does-it-change-the-fpl-landscape">Welbeck to Chelsea – how does it change the FPL landscape?</a></li>
</ul>



<p>Van Hecke has at least been replaced, but for now, it looks like Albion will be relying on <strong>Georginio Rutter</strong> (£5.5m) or <strong>Charalampos Kostoulas</strong> (£5.5m) to lead the line, which perhaps feels like a bit of a gamble.</p>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading">INJURIES OUT WIDE</h4>



<p>The problems in attack don&#8217;t end there. </p>



<p><strong>Yankuba Minteh</strong> and <strong>Kaoru Mitoma</strong> (both £6.0m) <a href="https://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/2026/08/17/early-fpl-gameweek-1-team-news-for-all-20-premier-league-clubs">are set to miss the start of the season</a>, which leaves the Seagulls desperately short of wide-midfield options &#8211; and now competing on two fronts.</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">BRIGHTON: SUMMER TRANSFER ACTIVITY</h2>



<p><strong>Key Transfers In</strong>:</p>



<figure class="wp-block-table is-style-regular"><table class="has-vivid-green-cyan-background-color has-background"><tbody><tr><td>MID |&nbsp;<strong>Zadok Yohanna&nbsp;</strong>|&nbsp;<em>AIK (£21.5m)</em></td></tr><tr><td>DEF |&nbsp;<strong>Costinha</strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<em>Olympiacos (£11m)</em></td></tr><tr><td>DEF | <strong>Pascal Struijk</strong> | <em>Leeds United (£20m)</em></td></tr><tr><td>DEF | <strong>Michael Svoboda</strong>&nbsp;| <em>Venezia (£4.3m)</em></td></tr><tr><td>DEF | <strong>Luka Vuskovic</strong>&nbsp;| <em>Tottenham Hotspur (£46m)</em></td></tr></tbody></table></figure>



<p><strong>Key Transfers Out:</strong></p>



<figure class="wp-block-table is-style-regular"><table class="has-blush-bordeaux-gradient-background has-background"><tbody><tr><td>MID |&nbsp;<strong>Jeremy Sarmiento</strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<em>Middlesbrough (Undisclosed)</em></td></tr><tr><td>MID |&nbsp;<strong>James Milner</strong>&nbsp;| <em>Retired</em></td></tr><tr><td>MID |&nbsp;<strong>Solly March</strong>&nbsp;| <em>Released</em></td></tr><tr><td>DEF |&nbsp;<strong>Adam Webster</strong>&nbsp;| <em><em>Released</em></em></td></tr><tr><td>DEF |&nbsp;<strong>Joel Veltman</strong>&nbsp;| <em><em>Released</em></em></td></tr><tr><td>DEF |&nbsp;<strong>Jan Paul van Hecke</strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<em>Tottenham Hotspur (£52m)</em></td></tr><tr><td>MID |&nbsp;<strong>Brajan Gruda</strong>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<em>RB Leipzig (loan)</em></td></tr><tr><td>DEF |&nbsp;<strong>Diego Coppola</strong> |&nbsp;<em>Paris FC (£15m)</em></td></tr><tr><td>FWD | <strong>Danny Welbeck</strong> | <em>Chelsea (£5m)</em></td></tr><tr><td>GK | <strong>Carl Rushworth</strong> | <em>Coventry City (£22m)</em></td></tr></tbody></table></figure>



<p></p>



<p>Brighton recruited three centre-backs over the summer: Vuskovic, Struijk and <strong>Michael Svoboda</strong> (£5.0m). We&#8217;ve barely seen Struijk and Svoboda in pre-season, <a href="https://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/2026/08/17/early-fpl-gameweek-1-team-news-for-all-20-premier-league-clubs#bha">with the former dealing with a fitness issue. </a></p>



<p>It&#8217;s difficult, therefore, to have a strong idea over which centre-back pairing Hurzeler will favour.</p>



<p>Vuskovic is the great hope. He averaged 12.5 DefCons per 90 minutes for Hamburg last season, and scored six goals &#8211; a fantastic total for a centre-back.</p>



<p>A new right-back in <strong>Costinha</strong> (£4.5m) has arrived; he looks very much like back-up to <strong>Mats Wieffer</strong> (£5.0m). Zero goals, zero assists and just 6.60 DefCons per 90 minutes in 2025/26 doesn&#8217;t set the pulses racing.</p>



<p>Similarly, the <a href="https://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/2026/07/02/who-is-brightons-new-right-winger-yohanna">exciting but very inexperienced </a><strong>Zadok Yohanna</strong> (£5.0m) is likely going to be understudy to Minteh and <strong>Diego Gomez </strong>(£5.0m) on the right flank &#8211; although the current injury crisis might fast-track his integration!</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">BRIGHTON: PRE-SEASON FPL REPORTS</h2>



<figure class="wp-block-table is-style-stripes"><table class="has-pale-ocean-gradient-background has-background"><tbody><tr><td>Jul 18 |&nbsp;<strong><a href="https://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/2026/07/20/fpl-pre-season-kostoulas-brace-chelsea-formation-hints"><strong>Brighton and Hove Albion</strong> 4-1 Wycombe Wanderers</a></strong>&nbsp;(h) |<em>&nbsp;Kostoulas (Minteh assist), Kostoulas (Osman assist), Osman (Keogh assist), Rutter (Boscagli assist)</em></td></tr><tr><td>Aug 1 | <strong><a href="https://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/2026/08/03/fpl-pre-season-gross-on-pens-mitoma-latest-garnacho-debut">Strasbourg 3-4 <strong>Brighton and Hove Albion</strong> </a></strong>(a) |<em> Gross pen (Wieffer assist), Boscagli (Gross assist), Cashin (Boscagli assist), Osman pen</em></td></tr><tr><td>Aug 8 |&nbsp;<strong><a href="https://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/2026/08/10/fpl-pre-season-vuskovic-bow-minteh-injury-ndiaye-pen-doubts"><strong>Brighton and Hove Albion</strong> 3-0 Roma</a></strong>&nbsp;(h) | <em>Rutter (Gomez assist), Ayari, Ayari (Rutter assist)</em></td></tr><tr><td>Aug 15 |&nbsp;<strong><a href="https://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/2026/08/15/fpl-pre-season-de-cuyper-oop-minteh-latest-hinshelwood-threat"><strong>Brighton and Hove Albion</strong> 1-0 Bologna</a></strong>&nbsp;(h) | <em>Hinshelwood (Wieffer assist)</em></td></tr></tbody></table></figure>



<p><strong>Form Players:</strong>&nbsp;Rutter (2 goals, 1 assist), Osman (2 goals, 1 assist), Boscagli (1 goal, 2 assists), Ayari (2 goals), Kostoulas (2 goals), Gross (1 goal, 1 assist), Wieffer (2 assists)</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">OPENING FIXTURES</h2>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><picture><source srcset="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-177-1024x100.webp 1024w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-177-300x29.webp 300w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-177.webp 1054w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" type="image/webp"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="100" src="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-177-1024x100.png" alt="" class="wp-image-174197 webpexpress-processed" srcset="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-177-1024x100.png 1024w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-177-300x29.png 300w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-177.png 1054w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px"></picture></figure>



<p></p>



<p>How you assess Brighton&#8217;s opening fixtures depends on your timeframe. Over the first nine Gameweeks, <a href="https://members.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/season-ticker/">they&#8217;re bottom of the ticker</a>.</p>



<p>Omit the trips to Liverpool and Man City at the end of that run, however, and it&#8217;s not looking so bad outside of Gameweeks 2 and 5.</p>



<p>Gameweek 1 could certainly be an opportune time to face Aston Villa, <a href="https://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/2026/08/17/early-fpl-gameweek-1-team-news-for-all-20-premier-league-clubs#avl">who are beset by fitness issues</a> &#8211; particularly in attack.</p>



<p>Gameweeks 10-17 looks a good period for investment, too:</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><picture><source srcset="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-178-1024x98.webp 1024w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-178-300x29.webp 300w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-178.webp 1051w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" type="image/webp"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="98" src="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-178-1024x98.png" alt="" class="wp-image-174205 webpexpress-processed" srcset="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-178-1024x98.png 1024w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-178-300x29.png 300w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-178.png 1051w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px"></picture></figure>



<ul>
<li><strong>READ MORE</strong>: <a href="https://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/2026/07/20/jump-on-jump-off-best-fpl-fixture-runs-for-all-20-clubs">Jump on, jump off: Best FPL fixture runs for all 20 clubs</a></li>
</ul>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">PENALTY + SET-PIECE TAKERS</h2>



&nbsp;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large is-resized"><picture><source srcset="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/image-3.webp 898w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/image-3-300x31.webp 300w" sizes="(max-width: 898px) 100vw, 898px" type="image/webp"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="898" height="94" src="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/image-3.png" alt=" 1" class="wp-image-74091 webpexpress-processed" srcset="https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/image-3.png 898w, https://cdn.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/image-3-300x31.png 300w" sizes="(max-width: 898px) 100vw, 898px"></picture></figure>



